## 🟠 Medium — Logic Issues

### 5. `freeShippingOnly` filter crashes on `AggregatorService` path
**File:** [facetService.js L70](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/server/services/facetService.js#L70-L72)

The filter checks `summary.lowestShipping?.isFree`, but products evaluated through `AggregatorService.evaluateProduct()` (dead code, but still) do **not** produce a `lowestShipping` property in the summary. Products built via `UniversalSearchService.evaluateCanonicalProduct()` do include it, so this only matters if someone re-activates the aggregator path.

---

### 6. SSE only triggers on empty brand/platform filters
**File:** [App.jsx L69](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/src/App.jsx#L69)

```js
if (searchTerm.trim() && !filters.brands.length && !filters.platforms.length) {
  connectSSE(searchTerm, activePincode?.pincode);
}
```

If the user types a search and also selects brand/platform filters, SSE live-scraping is **silently skipped** and it falls back to the regular `/api/search` endpoint. This isn't documented or communicated to the user — the "LIVE SCRAPING" progress bar never appears, which could be confusing.

---

### 7. PriceHistoryChart assumes `history.length > 1` for path calculation
**File:** [PriceHistoryChart.jsx L28](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/src/components/PriceHistoryChart.jsx#L28)

```js
const x = paddingX + (index / (history.length - 1)) * chartWidth;
```

If `history.length === 1`, this results in **division by zero** (`0/0 = NaN`), causing the SVG to render with `NaN` coordinates. The early return at line 8 only guards for `length === 0`.

---

### 8. Missing `helmet`, `compression`, `morgan` middleware usage
**File:** [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/package.json) vs [index.js](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/server/index.js)

`helmet`, `compression`, and `morgan` are listed as dependencies but **never imported or used** in `server/index.js`. These are security and performance middleware that should be applied — or removed from dependencies if intentionally unused.

---

### 9. `react-router-dom` installed but unused
**File:** [package.json L25](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/package.json#L25)

`react-router-dom` v7 is a dependency, but there is **no routing** in the app — it's a single-page view with modals. This adds ~50KB to the client bundle for nothing.

