## 🟡 Minor / Code Quality

### 10. `express-rate-limit` installed but unused
**File:** [package.json L18](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/package.json#L18)

Similar to #8 — `express-rate-limit` is a dependency but never applied. For a scraping-based API, rate limiting is important to prevent abuse.

---

### 11. `PriceHistoryService.generateHistory()` referenced but doesn't exist
**File:** [index.js L118](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/server/index.js#L118)

```js
priceHistory: product.priceHistory || PriceHistoryService.generateHistory(product.summary?.bestPrice?.price || 10000)
```

The `PriceHistoryService` class does **not** have a `generateHistory()` method. This will throw a `TypeError` at runtime if a product lacks `priceHistory`.

---

### 12. Silent `catch` blocks in scraper adapters
**Files:** All adapter `parseSearchResults` methods in [adapters/index.js](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/server/services/adapters/index.js)

Every adapter has `catch (e) {}` blocks that silently swallow errors. While this prevents one bad product card from crashing the entire scrape, it makes debugging impossible.

---

### 13. Platform filter UX inconsistency in `FilterSidebar`
**File:** [FilterSidebar.jsx L193](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/src/components/FilterSidebar.jsx#L193)

```js
const isChecked = !(filters.platforms?.length > 0) || filters.platforms.includes(key);
```

All platform checkboxes appear checked when no platform filter is active, but toggling one off actually **adds** the remaining ones to the filter array (via `togglePlatform`). This is unintuitive — unchecking one platform actually selects all the other ones.

---

### 14. No cleanup of SSE `EventSource` on search term change  
**File:** [App.jsx L63](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/src/App.jsx#L60-L93)

The effect *does* close the previous SSE connection (`sseRef.current.close()`), but a new search can fire before the previous SSE's `onmessage` callbacks have all been processed. The old callbacks will call `setProducts` / `setFacets` with stale data that momentarily overrides the new search.

